; ==============================================================================
; Disassembly of the Wizard of Wor ROM
;
; CPU Type: Z80
; Engine:   TERSE (Forth-like scripting language)
;
; Originally created with dZ80 1.50 on 02/19/02 by David E. Turner
; Updated & Corrected 2026
; ==============================================================================
;
; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; MEMORY MAP
; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  $0000-$3FFF  ROMs X1-X4 (Also Magic RAM area for hardware Pattern Board)
;  $4000-$7FBF  Viewable SCREEN RAM (Bitmap). Every line is $50 bytes long.
;  $7FC0-$7FFF  Non-viewable Video Margin. This $40 bytes is used for the Z80 STACK.
;  $8000-$AFFF  ROMs X5-X7
;  $B000-$BFFF  ROM X8 (Foreign language - normally empty socket)
;  $C000-$CFFF  X11 EMPTY SOCKET (Not used in WOW)
;  $D000-$D3FF  PROTECTED STATIC RAM (Requires $A5 unlock byte at port $5B to write)
;  $D400-$DFFF  Empty static RAM sockets. (Used as a temporary stack during boot)
;  $E000-$FFFF  X12-X13 EMPTY SOCKETS
;
; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; ROM CHECKSUMS & HOOKS
; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Note: The checksums listed below are 32-bit CRC hashes used externally by
; MAME to verify file integrity. Inside the original arcade cabinet, the Z80
; processor runs a much simpler 8-bit modulo-256 arithmetic sum to verify ROMs.
;
; Socket X01 wow.x1     $0000 to $0FFF, Checksum $c1295786
; Socket X02 wow.x2     $1000 to $1FFF, Checksum $9be93215
; Socket X03 wow.x3     $2000 to $2FFF, Checksum $75e5a22e
; Socket X04 wow.x4     $3000 to $3FFF, Checksum $ef28eb84
; Socket X05 wow.x5     $8000 to $8FFF, Checksum $16912c2b
; Socket X06 wow.x6     $9000 to $9FFF, Checksum $35797f82
; Socket X07 wow.x7     $A000 to $AFFF, Checksum $ce404305
;
; EXPANSION HOOK ($8006): During the boot sequence and diagnostics, the game
; checks address $8006 for the opcode $C3 (JP). If found, the game jumps to
; execute the external Diagnostic/Expansion ROM plugged into the high sockets.
;
; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; VIDEO MEMORY LAYOUT
; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Memory goes from left to right on the screen. $4000 is the top-left pixel.
; It continues right for $50 (80) bytes. $4050 is the left pixel of the 2nd line.
; Most writes to video memory are handled rapidly by the custom Pattern Board (DMA).
;
; Formula for printing to screen in double size mode:
; DE = ((line number - 1) * 960) + ((character position - 1) * 2)
;
; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; SYSTEM INPUT PORTS (Active Low unless noted)
; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; $08       Intercept register (Collision detector)
;             bits 0-3: Intercept in pixel 3, 2, 1, 0 since last reset
;             bits 4-7: Intercept in pixel 3, 2, 1, 0 in last OR/XOR write
;
; $10       System Inputs
;             bit 0: Coin Input 1
;             bit 1: Coin Input 2
;             bit 2: Coin Input 3
;             bit 3: Service/Diagnostic Switch
;             bit 4: Tilt / Slam
;             bit 5: Player 1 Start
;             bit 6: Player 2 Start
;             bit 7: Cocktail Mode / Flip Screen
;
; $11       Player 2 / Cocktail Controls
;             bit 0: Joystick Up
;             bit 1: Joystick Down
;             bit 2: Joystick Left
;             bit 3: Joystick Right
;             bit 4: Button 2 (Active HIGH)
;             bit 5: Button 1
;
; $12       Player 1 Controls
;             bits 0-5: Same mapping as Player 2
;             bit 7: Speech Status (Active HIGH - Chip ready for phonemes)
;
; $13       Dip Switches
;             bit 0-2: Coin slot pricing settings
;             bit 3: Language (Off=Foreign, On=English)
;             bit 4: Lives (Off=3/7, On=2/5)
;             bit 5: Bonus Life (Off=4th Level, On=3rd Level)
;             bit 6: Free Play (Off=Normal, On=Free Play)
;             bit 7: Demo Sounds (Off=Quiet, On=Demo Sounds)
;
; $15       Special Control Register 1
;             This port uses the Z80 'IN A, (n)' hardware quirk. Executing an
;             IN instruction places the Accumulator (A) onto the upper address
;             lines (A8-A15). The arcade hardware intercepts this to trigger
;             system latches.
;             Format: 0000 xxx y (xxx = function 0-7, y=0 activate, y=1 deactivate)
;             Functions:
;               0 = Coin counter 3
;               1 = Coin counter 2
;               2 = Star field
;               3 = Sparkle 1 (color 01)
;               4 = Sparkle 2 (color 10)
;               5 = Sparkle 3 (color 11)
;               6 = Audio 2 / Speech Enable
;               7 = Unused / Light Transistor
;
; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; SYSTEM OUTPUT PORTS
; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; $00-07    Color Palette Registers
; $08       Video Mode (0 = low res 160x102, 1 = high res 320x204)
; $09       Background color and palette split position
; $0A       Vertical Blank / Screen Height Register
; $0B       Color Block Transfer port
;
; $0C       Magic RAM Control
;             bit 7: Flip
;             bit 6: Flop
;             bit 5: Draw in XOR mode
;             bit 4: Draw in OR mode
;             bit 3: Expand mode (Convert 1bpp pattern to 2bpp colored sprite)
;             bit 2: Rotate 90 degrees
;             bit 1-0: Shift amount before copying
;
; $0D       Interrupt Vector upper byte
; $0E       Interrupt Enable (bit 3 = line interrupts, bit 1 = light pen)
; $0F       Interrupt Line / Horizontal Address Feedback
; $10-$18   Sound synthesizers
;
; $17       Votrax SC-01 Speech Synthesizer
;             This port uses the Z80 'IN r, (C)' hardware quirk. Executing this
;             instruction places the B register onto the upper address lines (A8-A15).
;             To speak, load the phoneme into B, set C to $17, and execute IN A, (C).
;             The phoneme is broadcast on the address bus while the IN strobe
;             tells the Votrax chip to read it.
;
; $19       Magic RAM Expand Mode Color
;             When the Pattern Board draws a 1-bit-per-pixel binary graphic
;             (like a text character) with the MREXP bit set in the Magic Register,
;             the hardware automatically expands each bit into a 2-bit pixel.
;             This port tells the hardware which palette colors to use for the
;             0s and 1s during that expansion.
;
; $5B       Protected RAM Unlock Port (Requires value $A5 before writing to NVRAM)
;
; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; PATTERN BOARD (DMA) PORTS
; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; $78       LSB of source address
; $79       MSB of source address
; $7A       Pattern Board Status / Line offset value
; $7B       LSB of destination address
; $7C       MSB of destination address
; $7D       Width of pattern
; $7E       Height of pattern (Writing to this port triggers the transfer!)